From 330fb4148bc4f5c83d7d0fe26036c5fc79996892 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Circelli <ryancircelli@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:41:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test(ipc): check the IPC message layouts on the host

The layout bugs so far only showed on hardware: bsd Socket's domain as a
u8 with stale padding, sm RegisterService in CMIF order over TIPC, Poll
and Select without the fd count and separate in/out buffers, the ldn
Scan filter read at offset 2, a one-entry indexed receive list that made
the kernel reject X descriptors with index >= 1, and auto-select out
buffers sized from C descriptors the kernel never delivers.

crates/ipc-tests builds nx's IPC layer for the host from a second crate
root, vendor/nx/src/ipc_host.rs, over the production sources. Only what
needs the console is swapped: the thread-local region, the system tick,
the heap/entry glue, and svc/asm.rs (svc.rs picks ipc_host/svc_asm.rs off
aarch64; the Switch ELF is unchanged). The SVCs the IPC layer issues go
to ipc_host/kernel.rs, a model of Mesosphere: it delivers a request as
the kernel does (no C descriptors, X data placed by the server's receive
list, the client's pid written in), records replies and what clients
send, and hands contended mutexes over as svcArbitrateUnlock does.

The tests drive nx's real client and ServerManager with the module's own
interface definitions (crates/sys/src/*/ifaces.rs, net/ipc.rs) and
compare against an independent HIPC/CMIF/TIPC codec and per-command
argument structs written from libnx (bsd.c, sm.c, ldn.c, nifm.c, time.c,
cmif.h, hipc.h, tipc.h), Atmosphere (sm extensions, kernel receive
lists, HipcCommandProcessor), Switchbrew and Ryujinx, and the overlay's
ldnt:cfg client. All values are synthetic. bug1..bug7 tests fail on the
code before each fix (bug 6, domain replies on the forwarding path, is
covered in crates/core).

make test-ipc runs them; CI caches the crate.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Circelli <ryancircelli@gmail.com>
